# C32 remediation after attempt-17 (9/8/9/8/8, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 a send the core took and then gave back was settled as delivered | The core now reports whether it gave a named send back: `TakenSubmission.returned`, set where a send's message is returned (`keep_unsent`, used by a declined write reconfirmation, a stop overtaking a renewal and `give_back`, and the failed-renewal path), matched by the send's entry (the newest not yet returned, since a returned entry number is reused). A repeated delivery of a returned send is refused, never sent. The page settles a reported send by what the core says: delivered, it leaves "Not confirmed" and clears the box only if it holds exactly that text; returned, it leaves "Not confirmed" without clearing anything, and its exact text stays in the box or is kept (once) under Not sent, also when the core's `unsent` field was never observed. The returned-message banner now says where the text is (in the box, under Not sent, or neither when the operator edited it away), never "kept under Not sent" while it is in the box. Tests: "a send whose receipt was lost and that the core then gave back is never taken as delivered…" (a failed renewal with the text in the box, edited further across renders and navigation; a declined write reconfirmation with a newer draft, the message kept once under Not sent across navigation; and a give-back whose unsent text was never observed; each in one coalesced snapshot, nothing resent; fails without the fix); `a_refused_renewal_gives_the_message_back_and_a_new_sign_in_continues` now names its send and checks it is reported returned and a repeated delivery refused; the submission-ordering regressions are retained | `harness_domain.rs`, `client.ts`, generated `TakenSubmission`, `harness.tsx`, `copy.ts`, provenance P50 |
| S1 a retired contextual read still reported the generic refusal | The read is dispatched apart from `run()`: it never holds the page busy or sets the page's problem; only the read still in progress reports its own outcome. The S1 test now also checks that no alert (including the generic "busy") appears | `harness.tsx`, `harness.test.tsx` |

Attempt-17's first check run kept two core-fixture flake logs from timing-sensitive tests outside C32; the final full-suite pass is on the same inputs.

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).

The first attempt-18 check run failed `context_credentials::transport::dropping_a_request_releases_its_connection` (a C02 test) three times in a row, and it failed alone too: on this machine's current network the TLS connection set-up took longer than the test's fixed 500 ms, so the request was dropped before the synthetic service had read it and no client close was counted (raising the window to 5 s passed). The test now drops the request once the service has it (waiting up to 30 s for that, failing if the request is answered instead), then expects the client's close; the whole `context_credentials` target passed three times in a row. No product code changed; the native record is unaffected.
